  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "The Evolve phase (turn 4 for the first player, turn 3 for the second) is the game's defining mechanic—planning your evolve target 2 turns in advance is more impactful than any single card play.",
      "Shadow (card cost reduction) and Ward (must-attack) are the most impactful keyword interactions; build decks to generate shadows efficiently and protect key followers with Ward.",
      "Class synergy is fundamental: each class (Forestcraft, Swordcraft, Runecraft, Dragoncraft, Shadowcraft, Bloodcraft, Havencraft, Portalcraft) has distinct mechanics; learning one class deeply is more efficient than sampling all eight.",
      "In Worlds Beyond, the Story Mode provides free cards for each class that form the foundation of budget competitive decks; complete Story Mode before investing in ranked.",
      "Card Pack efficiency: open packs for the current expansion first; each expansion pack guarantees a Legendary within 30 packs via the pack opening pity system."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "エボルブフェーズ（先攻4ターン目・後攻3ターン目）がゲームの決定的メカニクス。単一カードプレイより2ターン前からエボルブ対象を計画する方が影響が大きい。",
      "シャドウ（コスト削減）とウォード（攻撃強制）が最も影響力のあるキーワードインタラクション。シャドウを効率的に生成し、ウォードでキーフォロワーを守るデッキを構築する。",
      "クラスシナジーが基本。各クラス（フォレスト・ソード・ルーン・ドラゴン・シャドウ・ブラッド・ヘイヴン・ポータル）は独自のメカニクスを持つ。8クラスを試すより1クラスを深く学ぶ方が効率的。",
      "ワールズビヨンドのストーリーモードは各クラスの無料カードを提供し、バジェット競技デッキの基盤となる。ランク戦に投資する前にストーリーモードを完了する。",
      "カードパック効率：現在の拡張パックを最初に開封する。各拡張パックはパック開封憐れみシステムにより30パック以内にレジェンダリーが保証される。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Choosing Your Class and Archetype",
        "body": "New players should select one of the three most beginner-friendly classes: Swordcraft (straightforward aggro and midrange), Havencraft (defensive with countdown mechanics), or Forestcraft (card-draw-focused combo builds). Each class has a distinct playstyle that dictates whether you prefer proactive board development (Swordcraft), reactive control (Havencraft), or hand-size-based power spikes (Forestcraft). The Story Mode for each class teaches the class-specific mechanics before ranked play."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Ranked Climbing and Deck Refinement",
        "body": "In ranked mode (Bronze through Master), track win rates per matchup to identify deck weaknesses. Shadowverse meta decks are typically posted in the community tier lists weekly; cross-reference your current build against tier 1 lists and identify which 3–5 cards are suboptimal. Craft cards using Vials (from disenchanting extra copies) rather than purchasing specific singles—targeted crafting from a single-class collection is the most efficient path to a competitive build."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Master Rank and Grand Prix",
        "body": "Master rank and Grand Prix events require awareness of the current rotation (which card sets are legal) and accurate meta prediction. In Grand Prix, draft picks from a limited card pool; the draft meta differs significantly from constructed and rewards players who can evaluate cards on power level rather than constructed synergy alone. Prioritize the highest-attack followers with Ward or Bane in draft for consistent defensive stabilization."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Over-evolving in the early game—each player has a limited number of evolve points; evolving on turn 3 or 4 purely to trade with a weak 2-cost follower wastes an evolve point that could determine a late-game swing.",
      "Not tracking the opponent's evolve point count—knowing when the opponent has no evolves remaining removes a significant threat layer from their game plan; track the count visually on the evolve button.",
      "Building the deck with too many high-cost cards—the average card cost in competitive Shadowverse decks is 2.5–3.5; decks with many 7+ cost cards will consistently lose before deploying their power cards.",
      "Disenchanting limited cards from past expansions—limited cards from out-of-rotation sets occasionally return to rotation or become legal in alternative formats; disenchanting prematurely wastes potential future value.",
      "Ignoring the sideboard for Best-of-3 formats—in Grand Prix and competitive events, optimal sideboard construction against anticipated top-tier decks provides significant win-rate improvements in Games 2 and 3."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "序盤に使いすぎる。各プレイヤーのエボルブポイントは有限。弱い2コストフォロワーとトレードするためだけにターン3か4でエボルブするとゲーム後半のスイングを決める可能性があるエボルブポイントを無駄にする。",
